> It's gonna be hard to debug these reports without config dumps because if ur using things like oh my opencode I can't make any promises at all as to what it will do.

Thanks for bringing effort to this issue. I don't have anything special in my Opencode `1.2.6` configuration, just a MCP server and I can confirm the behavior of more credits being consumed in long operations with a single prompt.

Anyhow, for reference the `opencode.jsonc`

```yaml
{
  "$schema": "https://opencode.ai/config.json",
  "mcp": {
    "context7": {
      "type": "remote",
      "url": "https://mcp.context7.com/mcp",
      "headers": {
        "CONTEXT7_API_KEY": "hakuna-matata"
      },
      "enabled": true
    }
  },
}
```

> It's gonna be hard to debug these reports without config dumps because if ur using things like oh my opencode I can't make any promises at all as to what it will do.

I've asked Claude to write a logging plugin for me.  ([It's not pretty but it works](https://gist.github.com/MarcoGlauser/86ba61fd0836bee851decb1a1bd09281))  I've had no other plugins installed.

This illustrates the issue I mentioned above, which I believe to be a bug. I ran everything with gpt5-mini to not waste premium requests and removed some tool calls for brevity:
